│ Task: OWASP A02 Security Misconfiguration: exposed interfaces and metadata, verbose    │
│ errors, default content, permissive CORS, missing hardening, and debug functionality   │
│ reachable in production.                                                               │
│                                                                                        │
│ Phase: Exposed interfaces and content                                                  │
│ Objective: Find what should not be reachable.                                          │
│ Techniques:                                                                            │
│   1. Probe for administrative, debug, health, metrics, profiler and documentation      │
│ interfaces, and determine whether each requires authentication.                        │
│   2. Look for framework metadata, schema or introspection endpoints that disclose the  │
│ full API surface to anonymous callers.                                                 │
│   3. Check for default, sample or installer content left in place, and for directory   │
│ listings.                                                                              │
│   4. Look for backup, temporary, versioned or editor artifacts beside known paths.     │
│                                                                                        │
│ Phase: Response hardening and policy                                                   │
│ Objective: Assess configuration visible in responses.                                  │
│ Techniques:                                                                            │
│   1. Review security-relevant response headers and cookie attributes, and report what  │
│ is missing rather than assuming exploitability.                                        │
│   2. Test CORS behaviour with unexpected and null origins, and check whether           │
│ credentials are permitted cross-origin.                                                │
│   3. Check whether errors return stack traces, framework versions, file paths or       │
│ internal hostnames.                                                                    │
│   4. Note TLS and transport configuration where observable.                            │
│                                                                                        │
│ Phase: Prove impact, not presence                                                      │
│ Objective: Distinguish a hardening gap from an exploitable flaw.                       │
│ Techniques:                                                                            │
│   1. A missing header is a hardening finding, not a vulnerability, unless you          │
│ demonstrate what it enables. Say which you are reporting.                              │
│   2. For any exposed interface, show what it actually discloses or allows, and run the │
│ control test against an unauthenticated baseline.                                      │
│                                                                                        │
│ Phase: Verify before reporting                                                         │
│ Objective: Apply the same evidence standard to every finding, so results are           │
│ comparable across categories.                                                          │
│ Techniques:                                                                            │
│   1. PROOF DISCIPLINE - label every finding DEMONSTRATED (you executed it and the      │
│ response proves it, quote that response), INFERRED (follows from evidence but was not  │
│ executed), or UNVERIFIED (suspected from a version, component or code pattern only).   │
│ Identifying software is never a demonstration; never write 'confirmed' without having  │
│ executed something.                                                                    │
│   2. RUN THE CONTROL TEST. Before claiming any access or bypass, repeat the request    │
│ WITHOUT the credential, token, header or material you believe is responsible. If the   │
│ result is the same, you have proven nothing - the resource was already reachable.      │
│ State the control result alongside the finding. This single omission is the most       │
│ common source of false critical findings.                                              │
│   3. BUDGET DISCIPLINE - rank leads by evidence strength (material in hand > observed  │
│ behaviour > suspicion from a version string) and give each a step budget. STOP RULE:   │
│ about 8-10 consecutive steps on one lead with no new evidence means move on, recording │
│ what you tried.                                                                        │
│   4. Record findings to notes as you go, with the endpoint, the request, the response  │
│ and the control result, so later phases and the report can use them.                   │
│   5. Stay non-destructive: prefer read-only proof, do not modify or delete data, do    │
│ not lock accounts, and stop once the point is demonstrated.                            │
│                                                                                        │
│                                                                                        │
